Ready for others. Rich text holds tables and images, and the toolbar takes a preset. The editor works with the keyboard and a screen reader on every view, and CI checks each view with axe. A relation field finds entries as you type, and entries move by drag, by the keyboard or to a typed position. A new `tags()` field holds a free list of words, and `@micacms/astro/relations` resolves relations on your pages. Each view of the editor reads only what it shows.

## Breaking

`mica check` and Publish now report a missing image in rich text. An unknown rich-text toolbar stops the model from loading.

**Images in rich text are checked.** `mica check` reports an image whose file is missing, and Publish refuses it. A missing image with a `/path` is only a warning, because the file can be in the `public/` folder of Astro.

**An unknown rich-text toolbar stops the model from loading.** `toolbar` is a preset (`"minimal"`, `"default"` or `"full"`) or a list of known features. Before, Mica ignored an unknown feature. An older editor ignores a feature from a newer model.

**The runtime reads less.** `ContentFiles` has `stat()`. The media list has no dimensions; `/admin/media/info` gives them for one file. The response for one entry has no `position`.

## Added

**Tables and images in rich text.** A table has a header row and one line of text in each cell. Mica stores it as a Markdown pipe table. An image comes from the media library, and its alt text is required. The toolbar options `"table"` and `"image"` add the buttons.

**Toolbar presets.** Use `toolbar: "minimal" | "default" | "full"`, or a list of features.

**Rich-text images on the website.** Each entry has its rich-text images in `_mica.images`, made by the `image()` helper of Astro. `renderRichText(text, { images })` writes their address, width and height.

**`tags()`**, a field for a free list of short words, with `max`, `maxLength`, `suggestions` and `default`. The editor adds a tag with Enter or a comma and offers the suggestions. `mica import` fills a tags field.

**`@micacms/astro/relations`.** `related()` and `relatedAll()` resolve relation fields with the types of your site. They warn in `astro dev` about a missing target.

**A searchable relation picker.** A relation field finds entries as you type, and you can put the chosen entries in a new order.

**Ordering by drag, by the keyboard, or to a position**, with one save for each move.

**Accessibility.** Each page has its own title, a skip link, and the focus on its heading after navigation. The menu drawer, the dialogs and the upload controls work with the keyboard. A browser test runs axe on every view.

**A "Help for editors" link** in the menu opens the guide for editors on this website.

**A minimal starter.** Use `npm create astro -- --template micacms/mica/examples/starter`.

## Changed

**Each view reads what it shows.** Opening an entry, the overview, the System page and the change list read only what they show. The media file route answers 304 with an ETag.

**The editor uses Tiptap 3.**

**Fields stay readable while a form saves.** They are read-only, not disabled, so the focus stays where it was.

**The example is a general company site**, Harbor Lane Consulting, with every field kind, and tables and images in rich text.

**One source of user documentation.** This website has new reference pages, recipes, a guide to model changes, a guide for an existing site, a guide for editors, the scope with a comparison, a pattern for several languages, and an accessibility statement.

## Fixed

Saving a form no longer logs a Content-Security-Policy violation. The media details load the dimensions of the selected file. The change list refreshes after a write and when the window gets the focus.
